                <pb facs="0680" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.0144/98</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1063</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegram No. 1047 of May 8, 7 p.m., relative to an attack made on May 1 by armed
                    Mexicans on an American patrol in the Big Bend district, I have the honor to
                    report that in reply to the Embassy’s representations, the Mexican Foreign
                    Office states in a note dated the 17th instant, that the group of armed men
                    referred to were outlaws, and that the Mexican Government has issued appropriate
                    orders to pursue them actively.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
